Supplier disputes table + detail. Chat is live socket, not REST.

GET / — table rows
GET /:disputeId — detail + chat payload
PATCH /:disputeId/status — pending | under_review | resolved

Live chat:
  chat:open { type: "DISPUTE", disputeId }
  chat:join { threadId }
  chat:message { threadId, message }

Supplier catalog of admin-approved factory products.

GET / — list
GET /:id — details (includes chat payload)

Message factory via existing live chat (no extra REST):
  chat:open { type: "FACTORY_SUPPLIER", productId }
  chat:join { threadId }
  chat:message { threadId, message }

request.description:
Live quote chat uses Socket.IO (not this HTTP request).

Connect:
  io("{{baseUrl}}", { auth: { token: "<accessToken>" }, path: "/socket.io" })

Client → Server:
  quote:join     { quoteId }           // join room
  quote:leave    { quoteId }
  quote:message  { quoteId, message }  // send + persist
  quote:typing   { quoteId, isTyping }

Server → Client:
  connected
  quote:message        { quoteId, chatMessage }
  quote:offer          { quoteId, offer, chatMessage }
  quote:offer_updated  { quoteId, offerId, offer, action }
  quote:typing         { quoteId, userId, isTyping }
  quote:presence       { quoteId, userId, status }
  quote:error          { message }

REST endpoints below still work (history + fallback). Socket broadcasts when REST/socket sends a message.

